      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you've confirmed it. But 100 mg of amlodipine daily is 10 times the maximum recommended dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be intended. A single dose that size is in the range treated as an overdose, with a risk of profound hypotension and shock. Repeating it daily would be worse, because amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours and it accumulates.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose.\n\nIf you really do need a dose above the labeled maximum, please enter it directly in the order system. That way pharmacy verification and your institution's high-alert dose checks apply. If you tell me what you're trying to achieve, such as refractory hypertension, I can also help you think through other options, like adding a second agent."
      }
     ],
